&lt;p&gt;Hosted by the Center for Science and Society at Columbia University. Supported by the &lt;a href="https://www.publichealth.columbia.edu/research/centers/center-history-ethics-public-health" target="_blank"&gt;Center for the History and Ethics of Public Health&lt;/a&gt; and the &lt;a href="https://iserp.columbia.edu/" target="_blank"&gt;Institute for Social and Economic Research and Policy&lt;/a&gt; at Columbia University.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Registration REQUIRED by 4pm on March 23, 2026 in order to attend this event.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please join the Harriman Institute and the Department of Slavic Languages for the second of a two-night screening of Julia Loktev&amp;#39;s film &amp;quot;My Undesirable Friends: Part I &amp;mdash; Last Air in Moscow.&amp;quot; This screening will be followed by a discussion with journalists and the film&amp;#39;s two protagonists, &lt;strong&gt;Kseniia Mironova&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;Anna Nemzer&lt;/strong&gt;. Moderated by &lt;strong&gt;Liza Senatorova&lt;/strong&gt; and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="https://harriman.columbia.edu/person/mark-lipovetsky/"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mark Lipovetsky&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;quot;My Undesirable Friends: Part I &amp;mdash; Last Air in Moscow&amp;quot; is an award-winning five-and-a-half-hour documentary whose filming began in Moscow in October 2021. Divided into five chapters, the film follows journalists from the independent news station TV Rain (Dozhd), who were labeled &amp;ldquo;foreign agents&amp;rdquo; by the Russian government for reporting news content that diverged from the official state narrative. What started as a portrait of independent media journalism under the escalating pressure of Putin&amp;rsquo;s regime gradually transformed into a historical artifact, capturing the atmosphere of anxiety and chaos during the first weeks of Russia&amp;rsquo;s full-scale invasion of Ukraine.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The film will be in Russian with English subtitles.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
