&lt;p&gt;Join CUIT Research Computing Services (RCS) for a session on practical ways that various cloud tools can be used in your research workflows. This in-person workshop, led by experts from Google Cloud,&amp;nbsp;will provide an overview of how Columbia&amp;#39;s researchers can integrate advanced cloud tools into their academic workflows to accelerate discovery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CUIT RCS and Google will highlight tools that are now integrated into LionMail&amp;#39;s Google Workspace, tools that can be used for a fee/credits, and available credit programs from Google. We will also reiterate data types that can be analyzed&amp;nbsp;in Google Cloud as per Columbia&amp;#39;s Data Classification Policy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Attendees&amp;nbsp;will be shown how specific tools (such as the Gemini CLI and Gemini in-Cloud Console) can be used or navigating, querying, and debugging research datasets. The&amp;nbsp;session will also include live demonstrations of NotebookLM for creating interactive knowledge bases and Vertex AI for scaling searches across custom document collections.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By the end of the event, researchers will have the foundational knowledge to implement scalable, AI-driven solutions in their own investigative projects.&lt;/p&gt;

